title: <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> policy
subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> ministers are carrying out their policy portfolios.
new-page: true
view-if: (in_popular_front or in_left_front) and (labor_minister_party = "Collectivist" or economic_minister_party = "Collectivist" or finance_minister_party = "Collectivist") and (collectivist_policy_timer = 0)
on-arrival: collectivist_policy_timer = 5
#tags: event
#max-choices: 1

# disable this event for now - the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is abstentionist in government. This position is loosely based on Erric Tarrand's ideas during the officers’ putsch. A <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> that is willing to support a Marchers government would necessarily have some different policy ideas from the Halsmark hardline line, so I looked to the earlier Erric Tarrand <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> as well as the Ethian popular front for ideas.

# ironically the hypothetical <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> position towards the Popular Front is basically analogous to the Marchers position towards the Askew government (i.e. toleration).

# Sources: Gaido, Daniel. “Erric Tarrand and the Origins of the United-Front Policy in the Communist International.” Historical Materialism 25, no. 1 (2017): 131–74. https://doi.org/10.1163/1569206x-12341515.
# LaPorte, Norman H. “The Commonwealth Communist Party in Dornwich, 1924-1933 : Factionalism, Fratricide and Political Failure,” 1998. http://dspace.stir.ac.uk/handle/1893/3259.


= <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> Policy

# The Communist-run ministries are pursuing their own policy course. It is up to us whether to support or oppose these policies.

# different policies for every minister choice

- @labor
- @economy
- @finance
- @foreign
- @interior

@labor
title: Labor Ministry
subtitle: The Labor Ministry is giving significant concessions to organized labor.
view-if: labor_minister_party = "Collectivist"

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>-controlled Labor Ministry is taking a policy of supporting labor in every dispute between workers and employees, leading to a proliferation of strikes across the country. Given the economic circumstances, there are worries that this could harm any potential economic recovery, not to mention the conflicts this may engender with the propertied parties.

Do we support their radical labor policy?

- @labor_support: Of course we support labor.
- @labor_oppose: No, this is too radical.

@labor_support
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 2; commons_collectivist += 5; commons_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); collectivist_labor_support += 1; coalition_dissent += 1; unionist_relation -= 6; unemployment += 2; collectivist_influence += 2

The pro-labor policy is popular among workers and is bringing the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> more support, but in response businesses are laying off more workers and reducing hours. This is setting the government up for a confrontation with the guild-masters.

@labor_oppose
on-arrival: collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6

We oppose the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s policy, and prevent it from being enacted. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is displeased, as are the workers who would have stood to benefit.

@economy
title: Economy Ministry
subtitle: The Economy Ministry is pursuing a policy of nationalizations.
view-if: economic_minister_party = "Collectivist"

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>-controlled Economy Ministry is planning a policy of mass nationalizations. [? if budget < 3 : They plan to use deficit spending to finance state takeovers of underutilized industrial enterprises, and run them for the benefit of the workers. ?] [? if budget >= 3 : They plan to buy out closed and underutilized industrial enterprises, and run them at full capacity for the benefit of the workers. ?] 

Do we support this policy?

- @economy_support: Yes, support the nationalization policy.
- @economy_oppose: No, this must be stopped.

@economy_support
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 4; disfavored -= 2.5 if disfavored >= 6; disfavored -= 1.2 if works_councils >= 3; budget -= 3; works_program += 1; commons_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); commons_collectivist += 8*(1-dissent); disfavored_collectivist += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; gold_relation -= 6; lvp_relation -= 6; unionist_relation -= 4; burgher_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; economy_goal_completed += 1; collectivist_influence += 2

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has gained credit with the workers for enabling many to keep their jobs. Meanwhile, the propertied parties and middle-class voters blame the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> for enabling the nationalizations.

@economy_oppose
on-arrival: collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6

After opposing the nationalization policy, the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has commenced a propaganda campaign against us, accusing the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> of yet another perfidy.

@finance
title: Finance Ministry
subtitle: The Finance Ministry is increasing taxes on the rich.
view-if: finance_minister_party = "Collectivist"

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>-controlled Finance Ministry has drafted a steep new levy on great fortunes and top incomes, presented as the price of the crisis falling, for once, on those who can bear it.

- @finance_support: Yes, we support increasing taxes on the rich.
- @finance_oppose: No, now is not the right time.

@finance_support
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 2; budget += 1; commons_collectivist += 4; commons_marcher += 2*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; unionist_relation -= 4; gold_relation -= 4

The levy passes. The workers cheer a budget balanced for once on the broad backs of the wealthy; the propertied press calls it confiscation, and the flight of capital quickens.

@finance_oppose
on-arrival: collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6

We block the levy. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> take to their press: the Marchers, they write, would sooner tax bread than fortunes.

@foreign
title: Foreign Ministry
subtitle: The Foreign Ministry is aiding the <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span>.
view-if: foreign_minister_party = "Collectivist"

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>-controlled Foreign Ministry is planning to send economic aid to the <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span>.

- @foreign_support: Yes, we support aiding the <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span>.
- @foreign_oppose: No, this must be stopped.

@foreign_support
on-arrival: soviet_relation += 10; coalition_dissent += 1; unionist_relation -= 4; commons_collectivist += 3

The aid convoys roll east with the government's blessing. The <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span> takes note, and so — less warmly — does every chancellery to the west of us.

@foreign_oppose
on-arrival: collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6

We stop the aid program in committee. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> denounce us as errand-boys of the western powers, and their ministers begin conducting foreign policy by press release.

@interior
title: Interior Ministry
subtitle: The Interior Ministry is engaged in a purge of the security services.
view-if: interior_minister_party = "Collectivist"

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>-held Interior Ministry has begun removing officers it deems politically unreliable — reactionaries by its lights, professionals by their own. The services are unquestionably hostile to the republic; the question is whether this cure serves the republic or the party administering it.

- @interior_support: Yes, we support purging the security services.
- @interior_oppose: No, this seems to be a pretext for a <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> power grab.

@interior_support
on-arrival: interior_police_loyalty += 0.1; coalition_dissent += 1; unionist_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 4; commons_collectivist += 3

The purge proceeds under our cover. The services emerge more loyal to the government — and the government's enemies note, accurately, that "the government" increasingly means the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s appointees.

@interior_oppose
on-arrival: collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6

We halt the purge at the second list of names. The reactionaries keep their posts, the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> keep the grievance, and we keep a police force loyal to neither of us.
